                "ImageDescription": {
                  "value": "<p>A horizontal wooden beam with Roman numerals 'VIII' and 'XXXXXVI'.</p>\n<p>A master carpenter would label joints with Roman numerals so that the workers knew what logs to connect. One of the many places at Green Tree Tavern to find these marks is under the porch.</p>\n<ul><li>Keywords: vertical log; Ste. Genevieve; ste. genevieve nhp; colonial french architecture; Green Tree Tavern; poteaux-sur-sole</li></ul>",
